# Rust
/target/

# Documentation site
/site/
/.venv/

# Fuzzing. The seed corpus is not checked in either: scripts/fuzz.sh builds it from tests/programs/,
# tests/adversarial/, and fuzz/regressions/, which are already in the repository. A second copy of
# those files under fuzz/ would be one more thing to keep in step with them, and it would go stale
# the first time a program was added. What libfuzzer adds to the corpus during a run is
# machine-specific and regenerable; what it crashes on is minimized by hand into fuzz/regressions/,
# which is tracked.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Generated: insta's working files. A rejected snapshot is written beside the accepted one as
# `.snap.new`, and an inline snapshot's pending diff as `.pending-snap`; both are scratch for
# `cargo insta review` and neither is a record of anything once the review is done.
*.snap.new
*.pending-snap

# Generated: rustdoc staged into the docs site by scripts/build-docs.sh
/docs/api/
